+# Global model choices
+
+`scripts/models.mjs` stores user choices outside the plugin at `$CODEX_HOME/pstack-for-codex/models.json` (default `~/.codex/pstack-for-codex/models.json`). Resolve the script from the actual installed skill path. An explicit `--codex-home ABSOLUTE_PATH` selects an isolated destination without changing environment variables.
+
+```json
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "budget": "large",
+  "roles": {
+    "feature, refactoring": [
+      { "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoningEffort": "xhigh" }
+    ],
+    "arena runners": [
+      { "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoningEffort": "xhigh" },
+      { "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoningEffort": "xhigh" }
+    ]
+  }
+}
+```
+
+The saved file contains all 17 active roles. The helper fills missing roles with the packaged defaults and reports retired roles before dropping them on a requested save. A write may supply only changed roles; omitted roles preserve existing user choices. Each role is an ordered array. The 13 scalar roles contain exactly one entry; the four original list roles contain one or more entries. The four original multi-entry defaults stay length two; configured lists retain their actual length and duplicates. An alias entry is `{ "model": "auto" }` or `{ "model": "inherit-parent" }`, without `reasoningEffort`.
+
+## Commands
+
+- `read [--codex-home ABS]` returns `file`, `exists`, `sha256`, `config`, `targetReasoningEffort`, and `droppedRoles`. It never writes.
+- `resolve --role "ROLE" [--codex-home ABS]` returns `role`, `entries`, `source`, `file`, `budget`, and `targetReasoningEffort`. Use one subagent per entry for panel roles. The judge pool remains a selection pool.
+- `catalog --input ABS` normalizes native Codex `model/list` results or confirmed tool choices to `{ "models": [{ "model": "ID", "supportedReasoningEfforts": ["high", "xhigh"] }] }`. Collect paginated catalog results before passing them here.
+- `budget --budget unlimited|large|medium|small --catalog ABS [--codex-home ABS]` previews a full config while preserving role model choices, lists, and aliases. `needsChoice` lists entries without a confirmed effort at or below the target. This command never writes.
+- `write --input ABS --catalog ABS --expected-hash HASH|absent [--codex-home ABS] [--dry-run]` validates then saves a config or a `budget` command's proposal. Use the hash from the read that informed the confirmed choices. A stale hash, malformed preference, unconfirmed model, or unsupported effort prevents writing. Dry run validates the full proposal without creating a destination.
+
+## Invocation precedence
+
+The saved model entry overrides a consuming skill's default model. `reasoningEffort` is that role's resolved default under the selected global budget. A skill's explicit task-specific effort remains a deliberate override; validate it against the active native tool's supported efforts. Do not append an effort to a model ID. Both aliases select the literal parent model and effort and remain unchanged when the budget changes. Native `[agents]` defaults can replace omitted settings: omit override fields only when true parent inheritance has been established, otherwise bind the observed parent model and effort explicitly. If those values or that binding cannot be established, report the unresolved selection before dispatching. Follow the shared [Codex execution binding](../../poteto-mode/references/codex-execution.md) for the current native tool. Use the setup-managed, description-only `pstack-general-purpose` role for generic delegates so named role defaults do not override the selected settings; keep the original two file-based agents for their designated workflows.
+
+Native subagent tool names and argument names vary by Codex version. Bind the resolved values to the fields actually exposed in the current session; in the native spawn interface these are `model` and `reasoning_effort`. A full-history fork inherits the parent model; use a fresh-context task when the native tool requires it for explicit overrides and pass the needed evidence and absolute installed skill paths in that task.
+
+Budget affects default reasoning. Keep the original different-model and different-family review rules in the consuming workflow when assessing results.
